{
  // Dependency-vulnerability gate for CI (replaces the bare `npm audit --audit-level=high`,
  // which has no way to record a reasoned exception).
  //
  // The gate stays sharp: anything high/critical that is NOT listed below fails the build.
  // `allowlist` is per-advisory (GHSA id), never per-severity — we do not lower the level.
  //
  // Adding an entry requires, in this file: (1) the advisory id, (2) why it does not apply to
  // THIS codebase, measured — not assumed, (3) an expiry date, (4) what removes the need for it.
  // An expired entry is a task, not a renewal: re-check it, do not extend it by reflex.
  //
  // ✅ The allowlist is EMPTY as of 2026-08-08. Every advisory is answered by a version we
  // actually take. See "Removal notes" below for what used to be here and what killed it —
  // and, more importantly, for the two facts that are still load-bearing.
  "$schema": "https://github.com/IBM/audit-ci/raw/main/docs/schema.json",
  "moderate": false,
  "high": true,
  "critical": true,
  "allowlist": [],

  // ── Removal notes (2026-08-08) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Four entries were removed here. They are recorded rather than simply deleted because the
  // reason each one died is the same reason the next exception should be distrusted, and
  // because two measurements underneath them still constrain this tree.
  //
  // ## What actually happened: the exceptions did not expire — their REASONING went false.
  //
  // Every one of the four argued "no fix exists that we can adopt" (rule 4). Re-measured on
  // 2026-08-08 with `gh api /advisories/<GHSA> --jq '.vulnerabilities[]|"\(.package.name)
  // \(.vulnerable_version_range) → \(.first_patched_version)"'`, all four claims were false:
  //
  //   GHSA-qwww-vcr4-c8h2  react-router     claimed: fix only in v8 (breaking)
  //                                         actual:  7.18.2 — backported into the 7.x line
  //   GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg  brace-expansion  claimed: fix exists only as 5.0.8
  //                                         actual:  1.1.17 / 2.1.3 / 5.0.8 — every series
  //   GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895  brace-expansion  claimed: v5 only, 1.x/2.x unavoidable
  //                                         actual:  1.1.18 / 2.1.4 / 5.0.9 — every series
  //   GHSA-7p8r-x3mc-p8w7  fast-uri         claimed: only 4.1.2, outside ajv's ^3.0.1
  //                                         actual:  3.1.5 — inside ajv's range
  //
  // Advisories get re-scoped and patches get backported after publication. So an exception has
  // TWO ways to rot, and the expiry date only catches one of them:
  //   (a) the advisory stops applying   — caught by re-running `npm audit`
  //   (b) the stated reason stops being true — NOT caught by anything automatic
  // (b) is the dangerous one: the entry keeps suppressing a real, now-fixable finding while
  // every gate stays green. Check both at every touch, not just at expiry.
  //
  // All four were resolved by patch bumps inside existing ranges — `npm update` on the six
  // affected packages, no `package.json` change, no override change, 32 lines of lockfile:
  //   brace-expansion 1.1.16→1.1.18, 2.1.3→2.1.4, 5.0.8→5.0.9
  //   fast-uri 3.1.4→3.1.5 · js-yaml 4.3.0→4.3.1 · nanoid 3.3.16→3.3.18
  //   react-router(-dom) 7.18.1→7.18.2
  //
  // ## ⚠️ Still load-bearing #1: the scoped `brace-expansion@5` override must stay.
  //
  // `overrides` carries `"brace-expansion@5": "^5.0.8"` (the caret is what let 5.0.9 in). It is
  // NOT leftover from the removed entries — dropping it to a flat `"brace-expansion"` override,
  // or removing it so a v5 copy hoists, breaks the toolchain. brace-expansion changed its entry
  // point between v2 and v5:
  //     // v1 / v2                    // v5
  //     module.exports = expand       module.exports = { expand, EXPANSION_MAX, ... }
  // and minimatch@3 / minimatch@5 call the default export directly. Positive control, measured
  // 2026-08-08 in this tree (not copied from a sibling):
  //   node -e "const b=require('brace-expansion'); b('a{b,c}')"
  //     → TypeError: b is not a function   (typeof = object; keys = EXPANSION_MAX,
  //                                          EXPANSION_MAX_LENGTH, expand)
  // and the scope is doing its job — resolving `brace-expansion` from each installed minimatch:
  //   minimatch@3.1.5 → 1.1.18 · minimatch@5.1.9 → 2.1.4 · minimatch@10.2.5 → 5.0.9
  //
  // Note how this failure surfaces: NOWHERE on its own. In 2026-07-29 lint, the test suite,
  // knip and the Storybook build all stayed green while the override was broken — none of them
  // fed a brace pattern to a glob. "CI passed" is NOT evidence an override change is safe.
  // `tests/toolchain/brace-expansion-override.test.ts` is the only thing that answers it: it
  // resolves every installed minimatch and runs a brace pattern through each. Run it directly
  // before touching the override.
  //
  // ## ⚠️ Still load-bearing #2: js-yaml only moves because of a flat override.
  //
  // `@redocly/openapi-core` pins js-yaml **exactly** (`"js-yaml": "4.2.0"` in its
  // package.json), so GHSA-5p4m-2wfm-xmqj could not be answered by a lockfile refresh on its
  // own. It moved here only because `overrides` already carries a flat `"js-yaml": "^4.3.0"`,
  // which accepts 4.3.1. If that override is ever removed as "unnecessary", js-yaml silently
  // falls back to the pinned 4.2.0 and the advisory returns.
  //
  // ## Known remaining finding: esbuild GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr (low) — deliberately not fixed.
  //
  // esbuild 0.27.7, vulnerable range 0.27.3–0.28.0, patched at 0.28.1. It is **below this
  // gate** (`moderate: false`), so CI is green with it present — this is a recorded decision,
  // not an oversight. It is not reachable here either: the advisory is an arbitrary file read
  // by the esbuild **dev server on Windows**, and esbuild is absent from the production tree
  // (`npm ls esbuild --omit=dev --all` → `(empty)`, measured 2026-08-08).
  // It is not taken because it cannot be taken cheaply: `npm update esbuild vite` leaves
  // esbuild at 0.27.7 (vite's transitive pin holds it) while churning 367 lines of lockfile.
  // The fix rides along with a vite major upgrade. hub carries the fleet-wide vite wave on the
  // board (several repos hold the same low); do not open a one-repo bump for it.
  //
  // ## Prod exposure, measured 2026-08-08 (`npm ls <pkg> --omit=dev --all`)
  //
  // brace-expansion · js-yaml · nanoid · fast-uri · esbuild → all `(empty)`. Every finding in
  // this tree, past and present, has been dev-only tooling. Moderate count is 0, so nothing
  // slipped under the gate either.
  //
  // Full narrative: docs/development/dependency-audit.md
}
